<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Deiotarus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 40 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Deiotarus was a Galatian tetrarch who became king of Galatia in the 1st century BCE as a loyal ally of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a> rewarded his help against Mithridates VI with lands including Lesser <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a>. He sided with Pompey in the civil war, was pardoned by Caesar and defended by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cicero">Cicero</a> in 45 BCE, and by his death around 40 BCE ruled all Galatia.</p></div>
